START-OF-LOG: 3.0
CONTEST: CQ-160-SSB
CALLSIGN: OL1R
LOCATION: DX
CATEGORY-OPERATOR: MULTI-OP
CATEGORY-ASSISTED: ASSISTED
CATEGORY-BAND: 160M
CATEGORY-POWER: HIGH
CATEGORY-MODE: SSB
CATEGORY-TRANSMITTER: ONE
GRID-LOCATOR:
CLAIMED-SCORE: 222354
NAME: Radioklub Liberec
OPERATORS: OK1NY OK1MV OK1HGM OK2MTW OK1MER OK1FJX
CREATED-BY: DXLog.net v2.6.24
SOAPBOX: When the sun was very active before the CW part, we were looking forward
SOAPBOX: to SSB, where it should be works? At least according to the K and A Index.
SOAPBOX: The first hour was good with nice RATE of EU callers. The rest of time went
SOAPBOX: very slow and some hours has been very sleepy with couple of Qs per hour.
SOAPBOX: Again, we had a MULTI workplace where someone sat and looked at the
SOAPBOX: band map for MULT. Unfortunately, it's always complicated, if RUN doesn't
SOAPBOX: work, then you can expect a loss of frequency. The SSB part is strongly
SOAPBOX: unpopular for large QRMs and quite a bit of space on the band... The first
SOAPBOX: night was a total disaster on the US station, we made only 7 States, the
SOAPBOX: morning peak helped a bit, when HD8R called and TI1K was heard
SOAPBOX: beautifully. Unfortunately, the band map was full of stations, but almost
SOAPBOX: nothing gets through it. The night on Sunday without any exception.... Only
SOAPBOX: thanks for patience to K1ZM and K3ZM and that is from this year.
SOAPBOX: Probably nobody does remember such a bad conditions ever since last
SOAPBOX: solar maximum.
SOAPBOX: On the first night, unfortunately, we lost the BEV ANT 320m on the JA
SOAPBOX: direction, when the young men ran over the wire by his car. The next day we
SOAPBOX: were looking for the pieces of wire on the airport runway area and connect.
SOAPBOX: This BEV must be dismantled at sunrise and put back again after sunset.
SOAPBOX: Since the flying season started earlier this year, we had to go into the field
SOAPBOX: very quickly after Sunset. I think the test was more of a friendly an eyeball
SOAPBOX: QSO. Beautiful weather all weekend, really it hasn't been so nice for
SOAPBOX: several years in a row on the SSB part.
SOAPBOX: SETUP: RUN DX101D +PA, MULT DX10 + PA
SOAPBOX: RX: 320m double US BEV, Single 320m JA, 4x. Bidirectional SW/NE and
SOAPBOX: N/S.
SOAPBOX: Thank you all for the QSOs and patience to call us and repeated the SOAPBOX: callsign.
SOAPBOX: We had a fell like “Peeing against the solar wind” ...
SOAPBOX: Thank you all for the QSOs and patience to call us and repeated the SOAPBOX: callsign.
SOAPBOX: Also big thanks to Aeroclub Hodkovice for their outstanding
SOAPBOX: accommodation and hosting us for many years.
SOAPBOX: See you next time in the contest from anywhere.
SOAPBOX: Take care.
SOAPBOX: 73!
SOAPBOX: OL1R
